From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Domack <patrickdk@patrickdk.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:30:04 -0500
Subject: net: phy: realtek: set RTL826x short reach on high backoff

On a 3 ft cable an RTL8261N negotiated a local TX power backoff of
12 dB, and its switch-side link partner then requested a fast retrain
once or twice a minute. With short reach mode, 1.131 bit 0, set and the
link renegotiated, that unit saw no partner fast retrains and no PCS
errors in 15 minutes, against 20 in the 15 minutes before. The backoff
still read 12 dB local and 10 dB partner afterwards, 1.131 = 0xb801.
Links on 70 ft cables negotiate 10 dB and must stay as they are.

A board opts in per PHY with the device tree property
realtek,short-reach-backoff-db, the local backoff in dB from which to
switch. 1.131 encodes the backoff in 2 dB steps from 0 to 14 dB, so the
property takes an even value from 0 to 14. 0 turns the rule off, like
an absent property. Any other value, or a property that does not read
as a u32, gets one warning at probe and leaves the rule off. Like
realtek,enable-pma-low-power it has no binding document, as the RTL826x
support it belongs to is not in mainline.

On every link-up, while the property is set, the driver reads 1.129
and 1.131. If the link runs at 10G, the link partner information is
valid, autonegotiation is on, short reach mode is off and the local
backoff in 1.131 bits 12:10 is at least the property, a delayed work
sets bit 0 with a read-modify-write, reads it back and restarts
autonegotiation. 1.131 is a Clause 55 register, so links at 5G and
below are left alone, which also leaves the 5G-only RTL8251L and
RTL8254B alone. The work takes phydev->lock, checks autonegotiation
again, and does nothing unless the PHY is in NOLINK or RUNNING, so
read_status() never writes and the phylib state machine is never
re-entered.

The rule looks at the local backoff, not the partner's or the larger of
the two. During 10GBASE-T startup each receiver asks its link partner to
back off by an amount that depends on the signal it receives (55.4.3.1).
A local backoff of 12 dB means the partner's receiver asked for it, and
that receiver is the one that kept requesting fast retrains. The partner
backoff read 10 dB on both the 3 ft and the 70 ft links, so it does not
tell them apart.

Each flip is checked, so a bit the PHY does not keep cannot cause a
loop. If bit 0 does not read back as set, or the renegotiated link comes
up with it clear, the driver leaves the feature off until config_init()
runs. The renegotiation gets a 15 s window. If the window ends without
a link-up, or the link comes back below 10G, the driver clears the bit,
restarts autonegotiation and latches off the same way. It does the same
if the short reach link drops within 60 s of coming up. The driver
times that from the drop itself, so interrupt mode gets the same 60 s
as polling mode. A drop after 743's work had to reset the SerDes for
that link-up is the SerDes problem 743 handles, not an unstable link,
and goes to the outage rule below.

In polling mode the driver decides a deadline at phylib's first poll at
or after it, from the link state and speed that poll read. In interrupt
mode the work decides at the deadline from phylib's link state. When
that is down it reads 1.129, whose bit 0 is 0 while the PMA link fails
and does not latch, in case a 10G link-up is still waiting for its
interrupt. A failed read is retried a second later, and a clear that
fails is retried every 15 s.

Outside a window, a link that stays down for 15 s with the bit the
driver set gets the bit cleared and autonegotiation restarted, without
the latch, and the next link-up decides again from the backoff it
negotiates. A link partner reboot thus ends with short reach back on
after one extra renegotiation, and a swap to a long cable ends with it
off. The third such clear within an hour latches the feature off. That
bounds a link that trains in short reach mode but cannot hold it to a
few extra renegotiations, after which it stays in normal mode. The
clocks use 64-bit jiffies, so they also hold on 32-bit kernels.

After phy_stop(), or a suspend whose resume does not initialize the
PHY again, the driver has not seen how the link went down. phylib then
calls read_status() in PHY_UP when the state machine starts again, and
the driver takes that call as the start of a new run. It forgets the
link state and the 60 s hold from before. If the PHY starts again with
the driver's bit set and no link, the outage clock runs as for any
drop, so a port that comes back on another cable does not stay down.

config_init() runs whenever phylib initializes the PHY, on attach and
on resume, and on MACs that attach the PHY in ndo_open on every
interface up. If 1.131 bit 0 is set there and the driver set it, it
clears the bit before autonegotiation starts, because the cable may
have changed while the interface was down. Either way config_init()
re-arms the feature, so the next link-up decides again from the
backoff it negotiates.

15 s is several times the 2 s that 55.4.5.2 allows the 10GBASE-T
startup through maxwait_timer, with room for autonegotiation and
phylib's 1 s polling, so a link that can train comes up well inside it.
A link that fails within a minute of training is not a working short
reach link, while a partner reboot that soon after a flip is unlikely.
Three outage clears in an hour still allow a reboot and a cable move,
and stop a failing link after three extra renegotiations.

Seven new statistics show the state. Five are counts.
short_reach_auto_set counts the flips, short_reach_fallback the flips
that brought no 10G link up in the window, short_reach_not_kept the
bits that did not stay set, short_reach_unstable the latches for an
early drop or repeated outages, and short_reach_cleared_outage the
clears after an outage. The other two are state the counts cannot
show. short_reach_active is 1 while a bit the driver set is in force,
which short_reach_mode cannot tell apart from a bit that firmware or a
user set. short_reach_latched_off is 1 while the feature is latched off
until config_init(), which the latch counters cannot show once a
re-arm has cleared the latch.

Like 744, this applies on top of 742 "net: phy: realtek: add 5G and
10G PHY support" and 743 "net: phy: realtek: reset RTL8261N USXGMII
SerDes on link up", which are not in mainline yet.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Domack <patrickdk@patrickdk.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h      |   29 +
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c |  485 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 513 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
@@ -22,6 +22,33 @@ struct rtl826x_stats {
 	bool pcs_hi_present;
 };
 
+struct rtl826x_sr {
+	u64 deadline;
+	u64 up_since;
+	u64 clears_since;
+	u64 polled;
+	u64 auto_set;
+	u64 fallback;
+	u64 cleared_outage;
+	u64 not_kept;
+	u64 unstable;
+	unsigned int clears;
+	u32 threshold_db;
+	int txpwr;
+	int rearm;
+	bool link;
+	bool check;
+	bool verify;
+	bool pending;
+	bool owned;
+	bool proving;
+	bool settling;
+	bool early_drop;
+	bool slow;
+	bool outage;
+	bool disarmed;
+};
+
 struct rtl826x_priv {
 	struct rtlgen_phy_patch_db *patch;
 	bool enable_pma_low_power:1;
@@ -30,6 +57,8 @@ struct rtl826x_priv {
 	bool sds_work_disabled;
 	unsigned int sds_retries;
 	struct rtl826x_stats stats;
+	struct delayed_work sr_work;
+	struct rtl826x_sr sr;
 };
 
 int rtl822x_hwmon_init(struct phy_device *phydev);
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -364,6 +364,17 @@ struct rtl8261x_fw_entry {
 
 #define RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB			2
 
+#define RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS			15000
+#define RTL826X_SR_HOLD_MS			60000
+#define RTL826X_SR_RETRY_MS			1000
+#define RTL826X_SR_CLEARS_MAX			3
+#define RTL826X_SR_CLEARS_PERIOD_MS		3600000
+#define RTL826X_SR_REARM			BIT(16)
+#define RTL826X_SR_REARM_UNKNOWN		BIT(17)
+#define RTL826X_SR_PROP			"realtek,short-reach-backoff-db"
+#define RTL826X_SR_MAX_DB			(RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB * \
+	FIELD_MAX(RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LD_PBO))
+
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Realtek PHY driver");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Johnson Leung");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
@@ -3359,6 +3370,443 @@ static void rtl826x_cancel_sds_work(void
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&priv->sds_work);
 }
 
+/* Some link partners keep fast retraining on very short cables. When a
+ * 10GBASE-T link comes up with the local TX power backoff at or above the
+ * "realtek,short-reach-backoff-db" property, set short reach mode and
+ * renegotiate. The renegotiation has RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS to bring a 10G
+ * link up. If it does not, if the bit does not stay set, or if the link
+ * keeps failing in short reach mode, clear the bit and leave the feature
+ * off until config_init(). A later outage of RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS clears
+ * the bit without that latch, so the next link-up decides again.
+ */
+enum rtl826x_sr_action {
+	RTL826X_SR_NONE,
+	RTL826X_SR_SET,
+	RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_FAILED,
+	RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_SLOW,
+	RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_UNSTABLE,
+	RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_OUTAGE,
+};
+
+static u32 rtl826x_sr_threshold(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &phydev->mdio.dev;
+	u32 db;
+
+	if (!device_property_present(dev, RTL826X_SR_PROP))
+		return 0;
+
+	if (device_property_read_u32(dev, RTL826X_SR_PROP, &db) ||
+	    db > RTL826X_SR_MAX_DB || db % RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB) {
+		phydev_warn(phydev,
+			    "%s must be 0 to %lu in steps of %u, leaving short reach mode off\n",
+			    RTL826X_SR_PROP, RTL826X_SR_MAX_DB,
+			    RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	return db;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_rearm(struct rtl826x_sr *sr, int txpwr)
+{
+	int rearm = RTL826X_SR_REARM;
+
+	if (txpwr < 0)
+		rearm |= RTL826X_SR_REARM_UNKNOWN;
+	else
+		rearm |= txpwr & MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT;
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(sr->rearm, rearm);
+}
+
+static bool rtl826x_sr_due(const struct rtl826x_sr *sr, u64 now)
+{
+	return (sr->early_drop || sr->slow || sr->proving || sr->outage) &&
+	       time_after_eq64(now, sr->deadline);
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_proven(struct rtl826x_sr *sr, u64 now)
+{
+	sr->proving = false;
+	sr->settling = true;
+	sr->verify = true;
+	sr->up_since = now;
+}
+
+static bool rtl826x_sr_link(struct rtl826x_sr *sr, bool link,
+			    bool serdes_reset, u64 now)
+{
+	unsigned long timeout = msecs_to_jiffies(RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS);
+	int rearm = READ_ONCE(sr->rearm);
+	bool queue = false;
+
+	sr->polled = now;
+	if (rearm) {
+		WRITE_ONCE(sr->rearm, 0);
+		sr->disarmed = false;
+		sr->outage = false;
+		sr->settling = false;
+		sr->early_drop = false;
+		sr->slow = false;
+		sr->clears = 0;
+		sr->link = false;
+		if (!(rearm & (RTL826X_SR_REARM_UNKNOWN |
+			       MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT))) {
+			sr->owned = false;
+			sr->proving = false;
+		}
+		if (sr->proving) {
+			sr->deadline = now + timeout;
+			queue = true;
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (sr->settling &&
+	    time_after_eq64(now, sr->up_since +
+			    msecs_to_jiffies(RTL826X_SR_HOLD_MS)))
+		sr->settling = false;
+
+	if (link && !sr->link) {
+		sr->check = true;
+		if (sr->proving)
+			rtl826x_sr_proven(sr, now);
+	}
+
+	if (link) {
+		sr->outage = false;
+	} else {
+		sr->check = false;
+		if (sr->link && sr->owned && sr->settling && !serdes_reset) {
+			sr->early_drop = true;
+			sr->deadline = now;
+			queue = true;
+		}
+		sr->settling = false;
+	}
+	sr->link = link;
+
+	if (!link && sr->owned && !sr->proving && !sr->outage &&
+	    !sr->early_drop && !sr->slow) {
+		sr->outage = true;
+		sr->deadline = now + timeout;
+		queue = true;
+	}
+
+	return queue;
+}
+
+static bool rtl826x_sr_decide(struct rtl826x_sr *sr, int stat, int txpwr,
+			      bool autoneg, int speed, u64 now)
+{
+	unsigned int local_db;
+
+	if (stat < 0 || txpwr < 0)
+		return false;
+
+	sr->check = false;
+	if (txpwr & MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT) {
+		if (sr->verify && sr->owned && speed != SPEED_10000) {
+			sr->verify = false;
+			sr->settling = false;
+			sr->slow = true;
+			sr->deadline = now;
+			return true;
+		}
+		sr->verify = false;
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	if (sr->verify && sr->owned) {
+		sr->verify = false;
+		sr->owned = false;
+		sr->settling = false;
+		sr->disarmed = true;
+		sr->not_kept++;
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	sr->verify = false;
+	sr->owned = false;
+	local_db = RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB *
+		   FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LD_PBO, txpwr);
+	if (!sr->threshold_db || local_db < sr->threshold_db || !autoneg ||
+	    speed != SPEED_10000 || sr->disarmed ||
+	    !(stat & RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT_LP_INFO_VALID))
+		return false;
+
+	sr->txpwr = txpwr;
+	sr->pending = true;
+	return true;
+}
+
+static enum rtl826x_sr_action rtl826x_sr_action(struct rtl826x_sr *sr,
+						bool link, bool autoneg,
+						u64 now)
+{
+	if (sr->pending) {
+		sr->pending = false;
+		return link && autoneg ? RTL826X_SR_SET : RTL826X_SR_NONE;
+	}
+
+	if (!rtl826x_sr_due(sr, now))
+		return RTL826X_SR_NONE;
+
+	if (sr->early_drop) {
+		sr->early_drop = false;
+		return sr->owned ? RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_UNSTABLE : RTL826X_SR_NONE;
+	}
+
+	if (sr->slow) {
+		sr->slow = false;
+		return sr->owned ? RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_SLOW : RTL826X_SR_NONE;
+	}
+
+	if (link) {
+		if (sr->proving) {
+			rtl826x_sr_proven(sr, now);
+			sr->check = true;
+		}
+		sr->outage = false;
+		return RTL826X_SR_NONE;
+	}
+
+	return sr->proving ? RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_FAILED : RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_OUTAGE;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_set_done(struct rtl826x_sr *sr, u64 now)
+{
+	sr->owned = true;
+	sr->auto_set++;
+	sr->proving = true;
+	sr->settling = false;
+	sr->deadline = now + msecs_to_jiffies(RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS);
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_not_kept(struct rtl826x_sr *sr)
+{
+	sr->owned = false;
+	sr->disarmed = true;
+	sr->not_kept++;
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_clear_done(struct rtl826x_sr *sr,
+				  enum rtl826x_sr_action action, u64 now)
+{
+	unsigned long period = msecs_to_jiffies(RTL826X_SR_CLEARS_PERIOD_MS);
+
+	sr->owned = false;
+	sr->proving = false;
+	sr->settling = false;
+	sr->outage = false;
+
+	switch (action) {
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_FAILED:
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_SLOW:
+		sr->disarmed = true;
+		sr->fallback++;
+		break;
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_UNSTABLE:
+		sr->disarmed = true;
+		sr->unstable++;
+		break;
+	default:
+		sr->cleared_outage++;
+		if (!sr->clears || time_after64(now, sr->clears_since + period)) {
+			sr->clears = 0;
+			sr->clears_since = now;
+		}
+		if (++sr->clears >= RTL826X_SR_CLEARS_MAX) {
+			sr->disarmed = true;
+			sr->unstable++;
+		}
+		break;
+	}
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct rtl826x_priv *priv = container_of(to_delayed_work(work),
+						 struct rtl826x_priv, sr_work);
+	unsigned long timeout = msecs_to_jiffies(RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS);
+	unsigned long retry = msecs_to_jiffies(RTL826X_SR_RETRY_MS);
+	struct phy_device *phydev = priv->phydev;
+	struct rtl826x_sr *sr = &priv->sr;
+	enum rtl826x_sr_action action;
+	bool link;
+	int ret, val;
+	u64 now;
+
+	mutex_lock(&phydev->lock);
+
+	if (phydev->state != PHY_NOLINK && phydev->state != PHY_RUNNING) {
+		sr->pending = false;
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
+	now = get_jiffies_64();
+	link = phydev->link;
+	if (!link && !sr->pending && (sr->proving || sr->outage) &&
+	    rtl826x_sr_due(sr, now)) {
+		if (phy_polling_mode(phydev)) {
+			if (time_before64(sr->polled, sr->deadline))
+				goto unlock;
+		} else {
+			/* 1.129.0 reads 0 while the PMA link fails and
+			 * does not latch
+			 */
+			val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+					   RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT);
+			if (val < 0) {
+				sr->deadline = now + retry;
+				mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq,
+						 &priv->sr_work, retry);
+				goto unlock;
+			}
+			link = val & RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_STAT_LP_INFO_VALID;
+		}
+	}
+
+	action = rtl826x_sr_action(sr, link,
+				   phydev->autoneg == AUTONEG_ENABLE, now);
+	switch (action) {
+	case RTL826X_SR_SET:
+		ret = phy_set_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+				       MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR,
+				       MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT);
+		val = ret ? ret : phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+					       MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR);
+		if (val < 0 || !(val & MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT)) {
+			phy_clear_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+					   MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR,
+					   MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT);
+			rtl826x_sr_not_kept(sr);
+			phydev_warn(phydev,
+				    "short reach mode did not stay set, leaving it off\n");
+			break;
+		}
+
+		rtl826x_sr_set_done(sr, get_jiffies_64());
+		phydev_info(phydev,
+			    "TX power backoff %lu dB, link partner %lu dB: enabling short reach mode\n",
+			    RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB *
+			    FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LD_PBO, sr->txpwr),
+			    RTL826X_PBO_STEP_DB *
+			    FIELD_GET(RTL826X_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_LP_PBO, sr->txpwr));
+
+		ret = genphy_c45_restart_aneg(phydev);
+		if (ret)
+			phydev_warn(phydev, "autonegotiation restart failed: %d\n",
+				    ret);
+
+		mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &priv->sr_work, timeout);
+		break;
+
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_FAILED:
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_SLOW:
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_UNSTABLE:
+	case RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_OUTAGE:
+		ret = phy_clear_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PMAPMD,
+					 MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR,
+					 MDIO_PMA_10GBT_TXPWR_SHORT);
+		if (ret) {
+			phydev_warn(phydev, "disabling short reach mode failed: %d\n",
+				    ret);
+			if (action == RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_UNSTABLE)
+				sr->early_drop = true;
+			else if (action == RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_SLOW)
+				sr->slow = true;
+			sr->deadline = now + timeout;
+			mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &priv->sr_work, timeout);
+			break;
+		}
+
+		rtl826x_sr_clear_done(sr, action, now);
+		if (action == RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_FAILED)
+			phydev_warn(phydev,
+				    "no link %u s after enabling short reach mode, disabling it\n",
+				    RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS / 1000);
+		else if (action == RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_SLOW)
+			phydev_warn(phydev,
+				    "link below 10G in short reach mode, disabling it\n");
+		else if (action == RTL826X_SR_CLEAR_UNSTABLE || sr->disarmed)
+			phydev_warn(phydev,
+				    "link unstable in short reach mode, disabling it\n");
+		else
+			phydev_info(phydev,
+				    "link down %u s, disabling short reach mode until the next link-up\n",
+				    RTL826X_SR_TIMEOUT_MS / 1000);
+
+		if (phydev->autoneg == AUTONEG_ENABLE) {
+			ret = genphy_c45_restart_aneg(phydev);
+			if (ret)
+				phydev_warn(phydev,
+					    "autonegotiation restart failed: %d\n",
+					    ret);
+		}
+		break;
+
+	case RTL826X_SR_NONE:
+		break;
+	}
+
+unlock:
+	mutex_unlock(&phydev->lock);
+}
+
+static void rtl826x_sr_poll(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	struct rtl826x_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
+	struct rtl826x_sr *sr = &priv->sr;
+	u64 now = get_jiffies_64();
+	int stat, txpwr;
+
+	if (phydev->state != PHY_NOLINK && phydev->state != PHY_RUNNING) {
+		sr->link = false;
+		sr->settling = false;
+	}
+
+	if (rtl826x_sr_link(sr, phydev->link, READ_ONCE(priv->sds_retries),
+			    now))
